[32mcontrol[0m[36m:[0m[32mmatch[0m [36msubject[0m[36m=[0m[36many[0m [36mbody[0m[36m=[0m[36mcommand[0m
Branch on a value against a sequence of cases.

The body is a block containing a sequence of arms, where each arm is one of:

 * [32mcase <value> {<body>}[0m matches if the subject equals [32m<value>[0m.
 * [32many <stream> {<body>}[0m matches if the subject equals any individual value produced by reading [32m
                         <stream>[0m (e.g. [32m$(seq 5 10)[0m or a list).
 * [32mis <type> {<body>}[0m    matches if the subject's type is [32m<type>[0m.
 * [32mdefault {<body>}[0m      always matches.

Arms are tried in order; the first one that matches runs, and the rest are 
skipped. If nothing matches, [32mmatch[0m errors.

This command accepts the following arguments:

 * [32msubject[0m the value to match against.
 * [32mbody[0m    a block containing the match's arms.

[4mExamples[0m
[32mmatch[0m [36m$x[0m [36m{[0m
    [32mcase[0m [36m2[0m [36m{[0m[32mecho[0m [36m"$x is 2"[0m[36m}[0m
    [32many[0m [36m$([0m[36mseq[0m [36m5[0m [36m10[0m[36m)[0m [36m{[0m[32mecho[0m [36m"$x is between 5 and 10"[0m[36m}[0m
    [32mis[0m [36m$string[0m [36m{[0m[32mecho[0m [36m"$x is a string"[0m[36m}[0m
    [32mdefault[0m [36m{[0m[32mecho[0m [36m"I don't know what $x is"[0m[36m}[0m
[36m}[0m

[32mcontrol[0m[36m:[0m[32mreturn[0m [36m[[0m[36mvalue[0m[36m=[0m[36many[0m[36m][0m
break execution of a closure command and optionally return a value.

The [32mreturn[0m command can only be used when inside of a closure command. Closure blocks 
can not break early using the [32mreturn[0m command. Do note that you can use the [32mreturn[0m command 
inside of a closure block which is nested arbitrarily deeply inside of a closure 
command, which will stop execution of all inner blocks and return the closure 
command.

This command accepts the following arguments:

 * [32mvalue[0m the value to return

[4mExamples[0m
[33m# Define a factorial command[0m
[36m$factorial[0m [36m:=[0m [36m{[0m
  [36m|[0m[36m$number[0m[36m:[0m [36m$integer[0m[36m|[0m
  [32mif[0m [36m([0m[36m$number[0m [36m==[0m [36m1[0m[36m)[0m [36m{[0m
    [32mreturn[0m [36m1[0m
  [36m}[0m [36melse[0m [36m{[0m
    [32mreturn[0m [36m([0m[36m$number[0m [36m*[0m [36mfactorial[0m[36m([0m[36m$number[0m [36m-[0m [36m1[0m[36m)[0m[36m)[0m
  [36m}[0m
[36m}[0m
[33m# Call the command[0m
[32mfactorial[0m [36m5[0m

[32mcontrol[0m[36m:[0m[32mschedule[0m [36minterval[0m[36m=[0m[36mduration[0m [36m[[0m[36minitial_delay[0m[36m=[0m[36mduration[0m[36m][0m [36m[[0m[36mcommand[0m[36m=[0m[36mcommand[0m[36m][0m [36m[[0m--schedule_at_fixed_rate[36m][0m [36m[[0m--once[36m][0m
Schedule events at specified time intervals

 * If a command is specified, timer will run the command at the specified 
   cadence.
 * If timer is used inside a pipeline, it will read one row of input at the 
   specified cadence and write it out again.
 * Otherwise, timer will simply write an empty row at the specified cadence.

If a command fails, the timer will stop.

This command accepts the following arguments:

 * [32minterval[0m               the interval between heartbeats.
 * [32minitial_delay[0m          the delay for the first heartbeat. If no initial delay is specified, use the 
                          interval parameter.
 * [32mcommand[0m                a command to run at each heartbeat.
 * [32mschedule_at_fixed_rate[0m (default: [32mfalse[0m) if heart beat delivery starts blocking, catch up by sending more 
                          heartbeats afterwards.
 * [32monce[0m                   (default: [32mfalse[0m) only schedule a single heartbeat. After that, exit.

[4mExamples[0m
[33m# Show one row of the pipeline output every second[0m
[32mfiles[0m [36m/[0m --recurse [36m|[0m [32mschedule[0m [36m$([0m[36mduration[0m[36m:[0m[36mof[0m [36mseconds[0m[36m=[0m[36m1[0m[36m)[0m
[33m# Wait for a second and then print hello once[0m
[32mschedule[0m [36m$([0m[36mduration[0m[36m:[0m[36mof[0m [36mseconds[0m[36m=[0m[36m1[0m[36m)[0m [36mcommand[0m[36m=[0m[36m{[0m [32mecho[0m [36mhello[0m [36m}[0m --once

