[32mcontrol[0m[36m:[0m[32mtry[0m [36mbody[0m[36m=[0m[36mcommand[0m [36m[[0m[36mr[0m[33m#catch=string] [catch_clause=command][0m
Execute a command, recovering from any error it produces.

If [32mbody[0m fails, execution of [32mbody[0m stops at the failing statement, and [32mcatch[0m (if given) is 
invoked instead, receiving a struct describing the error as its single unnamed 
argument: [32mmessage[0m (the error text), [32mtype[0m (the internal error variant's name, e.g. [32mIOError[0m), and [32m
command[0m (the name of the command that failed, if known -- empty otherwise). Either way, 
the error does not propagate past [32mtry[0m -- execution continues normally with whatever 
comes after it, the same as if [32mcatch[0m had been given but was empty.

This command accepts the following arguments:

 * [32mbody[0m         the command to attempt.
 * [32mcatch_clause[0m the command to invoke if [32mbody[0m fails, receiving a struct describing the error 
                (message/type/command) as its unnamed argument.

[4mExamples[0m
[32mtry[0m [36m{[0m
  [32mrisky[0m[36m:[0m[32mcommand[0m
[36m}[0m [36mcatch[0m [36m{[0m
  [36m|[0m[36m$error[0m[36m|[0m [32mecho[0m [36m([0m[36m"Recovered: {}"[0m[36m:[0m[36mformat[0m[36m([0m[36m$error[0m[36m:[0m[36mmessage[0m[36m)[0m[36m)[0m
[36m}[0m

