Execute a command on a remote host

Serializes [32mcommand[0m (a closure), sends it over SSH to [32mhost[0m, runs it there in a fresh crush 
process, and returns its result. The remote host's key is checked against [32m
host_file[0m unless [32mignore_host_file[0m is set. Security note: setting [32mignore_host_file[0m disables that check entirely (no 
protection against a different host answering at that address); [32mallow_not_found[0m instead trusts 
an unrecognized host's key on first use and saves it, rather than erroring -- 
both weaken protection against a machine-in-the-middle impersonating the remote 
host.

This command accepts the following arguments:

 * [32mcommand[0m          the command to execute.
 * [32mhost[0m             host to execute the command on.
 * [32musername[0m         username on remote machines.
 * [32mpassword[0m         password on remote machines. If no password is provided, agent 
                    authentication will be used.
 * [32mhost_file[0m        (~/.ssh/known_hosts) known hosts file.
 * [32mignore_host_file[0m (default: [32mfalse[0m) skip checking the know hosts file.
 * [32mallow_not_found[0m  (default: [32mfalse[0m) allow missing hosts in the known hosts file. Missing hosts will 
                    be automatically added to the file.

[4mExamples[0m
[32mremote[0m[36m:[0m[32mexec[0m [36m{[0m[32mhost[0m[36m:[0m[32mname[0m[36m}[0m [36m"my-server.example.com"[0m [36musername[0m[36m=[0m[36m"alice"[0m

[32mremote[0m[36m:[0m[32mhost[0m[36m:[0m[32mlist[0m [36m[[0m[36mhost_file[0m[36m=[0m[36mone_of[0m [36m$string[0m [36m$file[0m [36m$glob[0m [36m$re[0m[36m][0m
