[32mremote[0m[36m:[0m[32mpexec[0m [36mcommand[0m[36m=[0m[36mcommand[0m [36m[[0m[36mhost[0m[36m=[0m[36mstring...[0m[36m][0m [36m[[0m[36mparallel[0m[36m=[0m[36minteger[0m[36m][0m [36m[[0m[36musername[0m[36m=[0m[36mstring[0m[36m][0m [36m[[0m[36mpassword[0m[36m=[0m[36mstring[0m[36m][0m [36m[[0m[36mhost_file[0m[36m=[0m[36mone_of[0m [36m$string[0m [36m$file[0m [36m$glob[0m [36m$re[0m[36m][0m [36m[[0m--ignore_host_file[36m][0m [36m[[0m--allow_not_found[36m][0m
Execute a command on a set of hosts

[4mOutput[0m
[32mtable_input_stream[0m [36mhost[0m[36m=[0m[36m$string[0m [36mresult[0m[36m=[0m[36m$any[0m
Like [32mexec[0m, but runs [32mcommand[0m on every host listed in [32mhost[0m (up to [32mparallel[0m of them at a time). pexec 
always attempts every host in the list, regardless of whether earlier hosts 
failed to connect or authenticate -- it never fails outright just because some, 
or even all, of the hosts couldn't be reached. A host that succeeds contributes 
one row ([32mhost[0m/[32mresult[0m columns) to the output; a host that fails contributes no row at all. 
Instead, the failure is logged as a warning (see [32mcrush:warnings[0m) naming the host and the 
underlying error. pexec's own exit status stays 0 either way, so the only way to 
tell whether every host succeeded is to compare the length of the output to the 
length of the [32mhost[0m list you passed in -- fewer output rows than hosts means some 
connections failed. The same host-key verification applies independently to each 
host -- see [32mexec[0m for what [32mignore_host_file[0m/[32mallow_not_found[0m mean for security.

This command accepts the following arguments:

 * [32mcommand[0m          the command to execute.
 * [32mhost[0m             hosts to execute the command on.
 * [32mparallel[0m         (default: [32m32[0m) maximum number of hosts to run on in parallel.
 * [32musername[0m         username on remote machines.
 * [32mpassword[0m         password on remote machines. If no password is provided, agent 
                    authentication will be used.
 * [32mhost_file[0m        (~/.ssh/known_hosts) known hosts file.
 * [32mignore_host_file[0m (default: [32mfalse[0m) skip checking the know hosts file.
 * [32mallow_not_found[0m  (default: [32mfalse[0m) allow missing hosts in the known hosts file. Missing hosts will 
                    be automatically added to the file.

[4mExamples[0m
[32mremote[0m[36m:[0m[32mpexec[0m [36m{[0m[32mhost[0m[36m:[0m[32mname[0m[36m}[0m [36m"web1.example.com"[0m [36m"web2.example.com"[0m [36musername[0m[36m=[0m[36m"alice"[0m

