[32mstream[0m[36m:[0m[32mfold[0m [36minitial[0m[36m=[0m[36many[0m [36mbody[0m[36m=[0m[36mcommand[0m
Accumulate a single result across all rows of input using a user-supplied 
closure.

[32mbody[0m is called once per input row, with the accumulator available as [32macc[0m and the row's 
own columns exported by name, exactly like [32mwhere[0m/[32meach[0m. Its return value becomes the 
accumulator for the next row; once the input is exhausted, the final accumulator 
is fold's own output. This is the general escape hatch for one-off aggregations 
that don't have (or don't need) their own dedicated command like [32msum[0m or [32mmax[0m.

This command accepts the following arguments:

 * [32minitial[0m the accumulator's value before the first row is processed.
 * [32mbody[0m    called once per row with the accumulator ([32macc[0m) and the row's own columns as 
           named arguments; its return value is the next accumulator.

[4mExamples[0m
[33m# Sum 1 through 5 by hand[0m
[32mseq[0m [36m1[0m [36m6[0m [36m|[0m [32mfold[0m [36m{[0m[36m([0m[36m$acc[0m [36m+[0m [36m$value[0m[36m)[0m[36m}[0m [36minitial[0m[36m=[0m[36m0[0m
[33m# Build a comma separated string from a column[0m
[32mfiles[0m [36m|[0m [32mfold[0m [36m{[0m[36m([0m[36m"{}, {}"[0m[36m:[0m[36mformat[0m[36m([0m[36m$acc[0m, [36m$file[0m[36m)[0m[36m)[0m[36m}[0m [36minitial[0m[36m=[0m[36m""[0m

