Calculate the sum for the specific column across all rows.

If the input only has one column, the column name is optional.

The column contents must be exactly one of the types [32m$integer[0m, [32m$float[0m, or [32m$duration[0m.

Normally, [32msum[0m expects the type of the column to be the type to sum over, but [32msum[0m can 
also sum over a column of type [32many[0m, so long as there is at least one row in the 
table, and all the rows are actually of the same type.

This command accepts the following arguments:

 * [32mfield[0m The name of the column to find the sum of

